# TypeUI in this project

When creating or changing user interfaces:

1. **Design system** — Read and follow `.cursor/skills/design-system/SKILL.md` (TypeUI **premium** registry). Prefer semantic tokens, explicit interaction states, and WCAG 2.2 AA.
2. **Fundamentals** — For hierarchy, spacing, typography, and a11y conflicts, read `.cursor/skills/typeui-fundamentals/SKILL.md` and its linked modules in that folder.
3. **Brand override** — For Thelliyankal client work, also read `.cursor/skills/thelliyankal-brand/SKILL.md` (warm luxury / rum & gold, not default blue primary).
4. **MCP** — If TypeUI MCP is connected (see `docs/TYPEUI.md`), use it to install design systems, UI prompt variations, and layout options before large UI builds.

Do not ship broken layouts (narrow column text, overlapping grids). Use an 8px spacing rhythm and 44px minimum touch targets on interactive controls.
